WEBVTT

00:00:03.780 --> 00:00:08.480
Oh? So ya finally hashed things 
out with your old BF, huh?

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:12.490
Yeah... though I sort of got dragged into it.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:16.240
Hey, you fallin' for Holmes-san or somethin'?

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:18.490
Wh-What?

00:00:18.730 --> 00:00:22.090
Holmes-san saved you when 
you were in a pinch, right?

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.300
And he's so darn handsome!

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.060
I bet he had you fallin' head over heels!

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.380
To be perfectly honest, 
I don't really know how I feel yet.

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.130
Aw, that figures, I guess...

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:36.300
That reminds me, Kaori.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:38.360
Do you have plans for next weekend?

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.390
Huh? I guess not. How come?

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.580
Do you want to go with me 
to Holmes-san's house?

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.770
Where'd that come from?

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:48.460
They're apparently throwing 
a birthday party for the owner.

00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:51.280
Every year, they invite 
all the people he knows.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.280
Holmes-san was hoping you'd come too.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:56.760
That sounds awful nice.

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:59.280
I'd be glad to stop by.

00:00:59.560 --> 00:01:02.060
Okay, I'll let Holmes-san know!

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:21.490
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:37.630
"The Connoisseur's Philosophy"

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:37.630
Episode 6

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.140
<b>The Philosopher's Path</b>

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:43.140
Holmes-san!

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.140
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:48.520
Aoi-san! Perfect timing.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.150
There's someone here I'd like you to meet.

00:02:51.150 --> 00:02:55.420
Kiyo-nii, is this your new part-time worker?

00:02:55.420 --> 00:02:57.780
Holmes-san, who is this?

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:02.870
A pleasure to meet you.

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:05.280
My name is Takiyama Rikyu.

00:03:05.280 --> 00:03:07.410
M-Mashiro Aoi.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.540
He used to work part-time at Kura, too.

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:15.090
He's been studying abroad in France, 
so we've been out of touch.

00:03:15.090 --> 00:03:16.550
Studying abroad?

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:19.230
<i>In France, so... music?</i>

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:21.800
Anyway, Aoi-san...

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:26.310
This is a good time for it, so let 
me make something perfectly clear.

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:29.050
Protecting Kiyo-nii is my job.

00:03:29.050 --> 00:03:32.010
Now that I'm here, you're no longer needed.

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:32.710
Excuse me?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.880
We appreciate everything 
you've done, of course.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.450
We hope you'll patronize Kura 
in the future. As a customer.

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:40.820
D-Does that mean...

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:43.070
<b>Fired</b>

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.560
I'm fired?!

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:47.680
Rikyu, don't be so darn mean to her.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.890
Just kidding.

00:03:48.890 --> 00:03:51.230
It was a joke, Aoi-san.

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:53.080
A j-joke?

00:03:53.320 --> 00:03:55.310
Forgive me, Aoi-san.

00:03:55.310 --> 00:03:59.380
Rikyu is like a little brother to me,
 so he can be rather wicked.

00:03:59.380 --> 00:04:02.090
Ah, I see...

00:04:02.420 --> 00:04:03.600
Let's start over.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.490
It's good to meet you, Aoi-san.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.350
Welcome home, Kiyotaka, Rikyu.

00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:17.970
<i>She's beautiful!</i>

00:04:17.970 --> 00:04:20.610
Yoshie-san. You've outdone 
yourself here, I see.

00:04:20.900 --> 00:04:23.770
It's a pleasure to meet you. 
I am Takiyama Yoshie.

00:04:23.770 --> 00:04:25.610
M-Mashiro Aoi.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:28.120
<i>Huh? Isn't "Takiyama"...?</i>

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.120
Yes, Rikyu is Yoshie-san's son.

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.870
But, um...

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:39.640
Despite how she may look, 
she's really in her forties.

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:40.880
<i>No way!</i>

00:04:41.150 --> 00:04:43.380
Mom's really something, isn't she?

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:48.620
Seiji-san told me that Kura 
hired a charming new part-timer.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.640
Seiji-san?

00:04:50.000 --> 00:04:53.140
Aoi-chan! Thanks for stoppin' by.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.140
O-Owner!

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.060
You look just as wonderful 
in Western clothing, Seiji-san.

00:04:58.060 --> 00:04:58.900
You bet I do!

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.130
<i>Wait, are they...</i>

00:05:01.130 --> 00:05:03.460
Yoshie-san is my grandfather's girlfriend.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:04.900
G-Girlfriend?!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.880
Th-That's quite an age difference they have...

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:09.290
But does that mean...

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.410
There's no need to worry about us.

00:05:11.630 --> 00:05:14.280
If Mom's happy, I'm happy.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:17.840
And I got to meet Kiyo-nii because of them!

00:05:17.840 --> 00:05:19.420
I-I see...

00:05:19.420 --> 00:05:22.280
Well, the party will be starting soon.

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.170
Go get changed, you two.

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:28.640
Um, could I go home to get changed, too?

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:30.890
You look perfectly lovely as you are.

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:33.180
<i>You don't have to do that every time...</i>

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:36.690
You'll be fine. Just leave it to me.

00:05:39.380 --> 00:05:41.190
It's just wonderful on you.

00:05:41.410 --> 00:05:43.740
Th-Thank you.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:47.030
It would be so nice to have a girl.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.570
Though my son is perfectly charming.

00:05:48.770 --> 00:05:51.110
You're amazing, Yoshie-san.

00:05:51.110 --> 00:05:54.580
You don't at all look like you
 might have a child in high school.

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:58.080
Seiji-san loves beautiful things, you see.

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:00.680
That's why I work hard.

00:06:00.680 --> 00:06:02.090
For my own sake, too.

00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.590
<b>Yagashira Seiji's Birthday Celebration
Congratulations on your 77th year</b>

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.270
Wow!

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:13.100
Oh?

00:06:13.610 --> 00:06:15.850
The Masamune boys are here, too.

00:06:16.180 --> 00:06:20.290
Masamune? The team famous for 
pantomime and impressions?

00:06:20.290 --> 00:06:23.360
He must have met them 
while he was doing TV.

00:06:23.700 --> 00:06:24.800
TV?!

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:26.350
Oh, you didn't know?

00:06:26.350 --> 00:06:29.370
Seiji-san used to appear 
as an expert appraiser

00:06:29.370 --> 00:06:33.370
on an antiques program 
called <i>Heirloom Hunters</i>.

00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:35.540
No one ever told me...

00:06:35.540 --> 00:06:38.120
I suppose he doesn't like to talk about it.

00:06:38.650 --> 00:06:41.560
Two years ago, on the set 
of <i>Heirloom Hunters</i>,

00:06:41.380 --> 00:06:44.130
<b>Heirloom 
Hunters</b>

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.880
there was some trouble.

00:06:43.320 --> 00:06:46.000
Ever since, he's said that TV 
is more trouble than it's worth.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.630
Trouble?

00:06:47.630 --> 00:06:49.610
Have you heard of Don Kageyama?

00:06:49.610 --> 00:06:52.360
Yes. The famous magician, right?

00:06:52.360 --> 00:06:54.390
I see him on TV quite often.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:07:01.270
Don Kageyama brought a family heirloom, 
a Joseon Dynasty blue-and-white vase.

00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:04.260
But Seiji-san immediately 
identified it as a counterfeit.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:07.480
It threw the whole taping into an uproar.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:12.160
The producer begged him, for the sake
 of the show, to say that it was real...

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:14.910
But you know the kind of man Seiji-san is.

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:20.410
He ended up declaring it a fake 
in front of the entire audience.

00:07:20.410 --> 00:07:23.220
Was everything okay?

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:27.380
Of course, Don Kageyama exploded. 
He said Seiji-san must be blind.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:31.810
Infuriated, Seiji-san announced, 
"I'm never doing TV work again!"

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:33.680
I-I can't believe it...

00:07:33.860 --> 00:07:37.640
The episode never aired, 
so most people never found out,

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:40.310
but it caused a lot of 
trouble behind the scenes.

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.940
Oh, speak of the devil.

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.940
That's the producer of 
<i>Heirloom Hunters</i>, Shimizu-san.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:49.690
I should go say hello to him.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.550
Of course.

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:53.450
Hey there, Aoi-chan.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:55.950
Akihito-san, you're here too?

00:07:55.950 --> 00:07:58.710
Don't you look lovely and mature today?

00:07:58.710 --> 00:08:00.380
Thank you very much.

00:08:01.030 --> 00:08:01.960
Aoi!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.210
Kaori!

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:06.460
Thanks for coming to... day?

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:08.980
Y-You're Kajiwara Akihito-san, aren't you?

00:08:08.980 --> 00:08:11.210
I-I'm such a huge fan!

00:08:11.770 --> 00:08:13.720
Thank you very much.

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.790
Kaori, you know Akihito-san?

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:18.050
You kiddin' me?

00:08:18.050 --> 00:08:20.650
He's a super-dreamy rising star.

00:08:20.650 --> 00:08:22.720
He's the hottest actor in the biz right now!

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:24.230
You didn't know?

00:08:24.590 --> 00:08:25.960
Kaori-san.

00:08:25.960 --> 00:08:31.740
The pleasure's mine to meet a girl your age
who can pull off Japanese clothing so well.

00:08:32.240 --> 00:08:34.280
Th-Thank you so much!

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.490
I'm always watchin' you on <i>Kyoto Days</i>!

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:39.490
Are you? I'm honored.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:41.650
I-It's nothin'...

00:08:42.250 --> 00:08:45.220
Kaori, I never knew you 
were such a trend-chaser.

00:08:45.220 --> 00:08:46.520
Aw, please!

00:08:46.520 --> 00:08:50.000
Us Kyoto-ites are all trend-chasers!

00:08:50.500 --> 00:08:54.390
Kaori-san, I'm going to take 
a picture with Masamune.

00:08:54.390 --> 00:08:55.320
Would you like to join me?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.260
Oh, I'd love to!

00:08:58.630 --> 00:08:59.590
Aoi-san?

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:02.880
What a surprise.

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.140
Did Yoshie-san provide 
your outfit and makeup?

00:09:05.330 --> 00:09:07.800
Y-Yes... Um...

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:10.150
Does it look strange?

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:13.650
Ya look just lovely. It's perfect.

00:09:16.900 --> 00:09:22.660
Everyone, thank you so much for coming
 to Yagashira Seiji's birthday celebration.

00:09:22.040 --> 00:09:27.290
<b>Yagashira Seiji's Birthday Celebration
Congratulations on your 77th year</b>

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:27.290
W-We have some of the Yagashiras' finest
 antiques on display in the exhibition room.

00:09:27.580 --> 00:09:31.040
W-We invite you to view them before dinner.

00:09:32.820 --> 00:09:34.850
Would you like to see them?

00:09:34.850 --> 00:09:35.740
Sure!

00:09:42.860 --> 00:09:46.690
Wow. So many expensive-lookin' antiques...

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:52.070
This one's... It's so beautiful.

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.080
This is a Chinese celadon.

00:09:55.080 --> 00:09:58.070
It's one of my grandfather's 
most prized pieces.

00:09:58.320 --> 00:09:59.280
Celadon is...

00:09:59.280 --> 00:10:03.950
Celadon is a type of pottery 
painted with a celadon green glaze.

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.580
It's known for changing in 
various ways during firing.

00:10:08.040 --> 00:10:11.140
Chinese celadons are considered 
masterpieces of the art form.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:14.200
Their beauty and refinement 
are simple, yet transcendent.

00:10:14.200 --> 00:10:16.340
Some even consider 
them aesthetic perfection.

00:10:16.340 --> 00:10:20.000
Only a few dozen have ever been identified,

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:22.850
so they're naturally incredibly valuable.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.820
Right, Kiyo-nii?

00:10:24.820 --> 00:10:27.600
I see you've been studying hard, Rikyu.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.350
Anyone who works at Kura 
should do at least that much!

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.160
Then I'll leave the explanations to you
 and head back to the party room.

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:39.860
Aoi-san, when you leave the room,
 would you mind locking up?

00:10:39.860 --> 00:10:42.370
Kiyo-nii, I can lock up!

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.080
I told ya already. That ain't your place now.

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:48.370
H-Holmes-san, you don't 
have to put it that way...

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.440
Kiyo-nii's so cool!

00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:52.630
Oh, never mind.

00:10:52.980 --> 00:10:55.380
Now, Aoi-san, can I count on you?

00:10:55.780 --> 00:10:57.380
Of course!

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:02.890
What? What is it?

00:11:03.100 --> 00:11:05.320
Look at that cool chandelier!

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:08.310
Wow, yeah! It's amazing!

00:11:09.440 --> 00:11:12.220
Ladies and gentlemen,
 the party is about to begin.

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.650
Would you mind joining us?

00:11:14.150 --> 00:11:14.950
Of course.

00:11:16.320 --> 00:11:17.320
Let's go.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:29.700
Okay, that should do it.

00:11:30.370 --> 00:11:33.930
Everyone suddenly left. 
Is something the matter?

00:11:33.930 --> 00:11:38.370
Huh? Well, the manager said 
the festivities were about to begin...

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:39.590
My father did?

00:11:39.590 --> 00:11:40.870
I see...

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:45.420
Well, everyone, thank you for comin' 
to celebrate this anniversary with me.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.420
Sounds like it's getting started.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.680
Then let us join them.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:49.930
By the way, Aoi-san...

00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.710
You should probably brace yourself...

00:11:52.710 --> 00:11:55.630
My grandfather's speeches 
tend to run extremely long.

00:11:55.630 --> 00:11:57.760
R-Really?

00:11:58.960 --> 00:12:02.190
Now, it's about time I wrap things up...

00:12:02.190 --> 00:12:05.370
I've made it to 77.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:10.120
I know I've only come this far with 
the aid of my family and friends.

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.960
So thanks a whole lot! Cheers!

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:14.620
Cheers!

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:22.840
The owner's speech really 
was long, wasn't it?

00:12:22.840 --> 00:12:25.840
Really? It seemed about normal to me.

00:12:25.840 --> 00:12:26.990
What, really?

00:12:26.990 --> 00:12:30.030
The owner's famous for his long speeches.

00:12:30.030 --> 00:12:33.850
If you can't endure those, 
you're not cut out to work at Kura.

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:37.610
<i>What does that have to do with Kura?</i>

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.990
Isn't that Shimizu-san?

00:12:39.990 --> 00:12:43.610
Just brilliant, Sensei! 
A fascinating talk!

00:12:43.860 --> 00:12:45.010
What do you think of—

00:12:45.010 --> 00:12:48.990
Shimizu-san, I'm grateful to you, and I 
know I've made a lot of trouble for you.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.360
But I won't appear on TV again.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.360
Come on, don't be like that!

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:57.130
The truth is, we're pitching a 
remake of <i>Heirloom Hunters</i>!

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.250
Today's my birthday party.

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:00.630
Don't go makin' me angry.

00:13:03.240 --> 00:13:04.910
<i>That looks pretty rough...</i>

00:13:04.910 --> 00:13:06.640
Say, Aoi-chan...

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:09.890
Who was that pretty gal 
you were talking to before?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.020
You mean Yoshie-san?

00:13:12.020 --> 00:13:14.050
So her name's Yoshie-san?

00:13:14.050 --> 00:13:17.650
She's gorgeous. Sensuous older 
girls are totally my type.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:21.150
Um, but Yoshie-san is...

00:13:21.390 --> 00:13:23.900
Excuse me! You need to stop that right now!

00:13:25.320 --> 00:13:26.300
Who are you?

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.800
I'm Yoshie's son!

00:13:27.800 --> 00:13:30.370
What? Don't be stupid. You couldn't possi—

00:13:30.370 --> 00:13:32.160
Akihito-san, it's true!

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:33.840
Oh, come on!

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:39.670
There's no way a beautiful young woman 
like her has a cheeky little brat your age.

00:13:39.670 --> 00:13:42.620
Um, Aoi-san, is he stupid or something?

00:13:45.690 --> 00:13:48.470
Hey, you hear somethin'?

00:13:48.470 --> 00:13:51.180
Sure did. It came from the exhibition room.

00:13:56.350 --> 00:13:58.440
O-Oh no!

00:13:59.640 --> 00:14:02.020
Wait! Were any of the other pieces...?

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.570
Everything else looks all right.

00:14:09.950 --> 00:14:12.960
Then why just the celadon urn, 
the most expensive item here?

00:14:12.960 --> 00:14:15.580
Do you think someone broke it?

00:14:16.120 --> 00:14:19.240
Aoi-chan, you locked the door, didn't you?

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:22.370
Yes. I double-checked, too...

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:27.080
Then who did this? And how?

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:29.340
Is something the matter here?

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:31.850
Holmes-san! It's actually...

00:14:33.240 --> 00:14:36.140
What's this? You're all actin' 
like someone died in here.

00:14:44.490 --> 00:14:47.490
Calm down, everyone. It's a fake.

00:14:47.830 --> 00:14:49.580
What do you mean?

00:14:51.440 --> 00:14:53.910
Kiyotaka'll explain the rest.

00:14:55.560 --> 00:14:58.810
The delegating keeps me 
on my toes, at least...

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:13.040
Well, this isn't a case of someone 
sneaking into a locked room.

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:18.270
In fact, the fake had already been swapped 
in by the time the room was emptied.

00:15:18.480 --> 00:15:20.770
You've gotta be kidding me, Holmes!

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:23.520
There were so many people 
in the exhibition room.

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:25.660
No one could have done something like that.

00:15:25.660 --> 00:15:28.580
They could... under certain conditions.

00:15:28.580 --> 00:15:29.780
Certain conditions?

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:33.030
One person to create a diversion 
while the other makes the swap.

00:15:33.340 --> 00:15:36.280
In other words, 
if there were multiple culprits.

00:15:36.640 --> 00:15:41.790
Culprit A points at something to 
draw the attention of the others.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:47.300
While they're distracted, Culprit B swaps 
the real thing with an already broken fake.

00:15:48.060 --> 00:15:50.050
B leaves the room.

00:15:51.160 --> 00:15:55.700
Then B imitates my father 
to lure everyone outside,

00:15:55.700 --> 00:15:59.060
mixes in with the crowd to sneak back inside,

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:02.950
and meets up with Culprit A. 
Then they leave together.

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:06.540
After making sure that the room is locked,

00:16:07.710 --> 00:16:09.970
they set a timer to play a sound,

00:16:09.970 --> 00:16:11.740
and the locked room mystery is completed.

00:16:15.120 --> 00:16:15.800
There it is!

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.470
Thank goodness! It ain't broke!

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:23.120
To accomplish this, the culprits would need 
skill in misdirection and impersonation.

00:16:23.360 --> 00:16:26.670
They also would have been the last people
 to leave the exhibition room.

00:16:26.670 --> 00:16:27.630
In other words...

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:31.630
It could be none other than Masamune.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:36.030
Hey, hey, what are you saying?

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:36.890
There's no way...

00:16:36.890 --> 00:16:42.020
Are you, by chance, affiliated 
with the magician Don Kageyama?

00:16:43.870 --> 00:16:47.270
Yeah. We owe Kageyama-san a lot...

00:16:54.010 --> 00:17:00.190
When we were living in the orphanage 
with no family, he showed us magic.

00:17:02.430 --> 00:17:04.140
He gave us hope.

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:09.540
So we wanted revenge on the man 
who called his heirloom a fake!

00:17:12.050 --> 00:17:14.050
You did this to get revenge on the owner?!

00:17:14.600 --> 00:17:17.870
We know that it was pointless.

00:17:17.870 --> 00:17:18.300
But...

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:26.210
When we thought about how Kageyama felt, 
we just couldn't help ourselves!

00:17:27.320 --> 00:17:29.690
Kiyotaka-san, we have a request.

00:17:30.040 --> 00:17:30.940
What is it?

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:33.920
Could we test you once again?

00:17:33.920 --> 00:17:39.200
I want to know if you people
are real connoisseurs or not!

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:41.840
Play me in poker.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:46.040
If you lose, you have to 
apologize to Kageyama-san!

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:50.290
Huh? It was a fake, 
so he called it a fake; that's all!

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.370
And Kiyo-nii has nothing to—

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:52.370
Very well.

00:17:52.370 --> 00:17:53.790
Kiyo-nii...

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:09.230
It's no use. I've lost.

00:18:09.480 --> 00:18:11.730
Hey, he's not even looking at the cards!

00:18:11.730 --> 00:18:16.240
Muneyoshi-san's hand contains two 
aces and three kings. A full house.

00:18:16.240 --> 00:18:17.740
And I have a junk hand.

00:18:18.100 --> 00:18:20.070
There's no way that I can win.

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.740
Wh-What's going on?

00:18:22.490 --> 00:18:24.730
The cards that Muneyoshi dealt...

00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:29.040
It looked like he was dealing 
from the top, but I could tell he wasn't.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.250
You mean he was cheating?

00:18:31.250 --> 00:18:33.880
This isn't a fair match.

00:18:33.880 --> 00:18:37.410
No way... He saw through 
Muneyoshi's sleight of hand...

00:18:37.410 --> 00:18:41.010
That counterfeit before, too. 
How stupid do you think we are?

00:18:41.410 --> 00:18:46.520
To my eyes, the work of an 
impostor is as clear as day.

00:18:46.520 --> 00:18:48.020
Damn you!

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:49.770
Holmes-san!

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:05.780
W-Wow...

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:06.790
Didn't I tell you?

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:09.540
I'll protect Kiyo-nii myself.

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:13.040
Rikyu, I see you've polished your 
skills further in your time abroad.

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:15.300
Then what you were studying was...

00:19:15.560 --> 00:19:17.550
Yeah, judo.

00:19:17.960 --> 00:19:19.800
<i>That's a surprise.</i>

00:19:19.800 --> 00:19:22.500
Rikyu. Release him already.

00:19:23.200 --> 00:19:24.300
Fine.

00:19:25.130 --> 00:19:27.930
Damn it! Who the hell are you people?!

00:19:28.320 --> 00:19:30.940
I'm a mere apprentice appraiser.

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:32.690
But...

00:19:33.840 --> 00:19:36.690
I won't have you makin' light of my judgment.

00:19:44.000 --> 00:19:45.700
That's enough, Kiyotaka.

00:19:46.960 --> 00:19:48.200
I'm sorry.

00:19:50.610 --> 00:19:55.460
I'm very sorry I embarrassed 
Kageyama-san in public.

00:19:56.230 --> 00:20:01.800
I truly regret hurting 
Kageyama-san with my words.

00:20:01.800 --> 00:20:02.970
Seiji-san...

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:07.970
That piece Kageyama-san brought in
 was a very well-made counterfeit...

00:20:08.350 --> 00:20:11.240
But a fake is still a fake.

00:20:11.240 --> 00:20:13.480
I can't go around callin' it the real deal.

00:20:14.050 --> 00:20:17.940
If I'd declared it authentic,
 it'd warp everything surrounding it.

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:21.240
One mistake by an appraiser
 can warp history.

00:20:22.260 --> 00:20:24.890
It's a heavy responsibility that we bear.

00:20:24.890 --> 00:20:27.990
So no matter how much you 
pay me, I'm awful sorry,

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:30.750
but I still can't say a fake is genuine.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.760
That's my philosophy as a connoisseur.

00:20:37.240 --> 00:20:42.510
We thought you did it because 
you didn't like Kageyama-san.

00:20:42.510 --> 00:20:45.840
But now we realize that we were being silly...

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:49.140
We made light of your judgment, like you said.

00:20:49.140 --> 00:20:51.020
We're sorry!

00:20:52.020 --> 00:20:54.270
I'm glad that you understand.

00:20:55.470 --> 00:20:58.040
Well, that's the end of that business.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:02.610
Seein' as there's plenty of booze and 
food left, let's get back to the party!

00:21:15.720 --> 00:21:16.790
Aoi-san.

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.020
Holmes-san...

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.960
I'm sorry about before.

00:21:20.960 --> 00:21:22.760
They just upset me...

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:25.760
<i>So Holmes-san can look this way, too...</i>

00:21:27.240 --> 00:21:31.260
Aoi-san, did you find me frightening?

00:21:31.720 --> 00:21:36.770
When my pride as an appraiser is on 
the line, I'm unable to hold back.

00:21:37.230 --> 00:21:40.020
No, I wasn't scared at all.

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:46.030
It just showed me how proud
 you are of the owner.

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:51.270
I thought it was really cool that you'd
 defend someone important to you like that.

00:21:52.110 --> 00:21:54.040
Thank you, Aoi-san.

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:01.790
<i>What the heck? Everything Holmes-san 
does today is breaking the rules.</i>

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:04.860
<i>Seriously breaking the rules.</i>

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:14.290
<b>Holmes of Kyoto</b>

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:52.080
Next Episode

00:23:36.480 --> 00:23:52.080
"Hesitation and Revelation"

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:40.680
This is my second time at a party...

00:23:40.680 --> 00:23:42.160
Aoi-san, anything you wear will—

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:43.860
You said that already!

00:23:44.580 --> 00:23:47.530
Next time: "Hesitation and Revelation."

00:23:47.530 --> 00:23:49.880
Holmes-san, you really are nasty!
